{"title":"2001 Pan African MO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_1\">Day 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Find all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/8/be82bae1c6366f386ccad61bfaefb45a87021066.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{n^3+3}{n^2+7}\\]\" width=\"50\" height=\"40\" />\nis a positive integer.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2001 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be a positive integer. A child builds a wall along a line with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> identical cubes. He lays the first cube on the line and at each subsequent step, he lays the next cube either on the ground or on the top of another cube, so that it has a common face with the previous one. How many such distinct walls exist?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2001 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be an equilateral triangle and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/1/241e6e35ad6d73fb2ef98244b0211deb2f25222a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> be a point outside this triangle, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/9/d29f795f355e054576b29f5d4ada6b1bfe8d1c8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{AP_0C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"63\" height=\"16\" /> is an isoscele triangle with a right angle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/1/241e6e35ad6d73fb2ef98244b0211deb2f25222a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" />. A grasshopper starts from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/1/241e6e35ad6d73fb2ef98244b0211deb2f25222a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> and turns around the triangle as follows. From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/1/241e6e35ad6d73fb2ef98244b0211deb2f25222a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> the grasshopper jumps to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b0256a78d58b6d5f7a53400b19e7747d2983fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" />, which is the symmetric point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/1/241e6e35ad6d73fb2ef98244b0211deb2f25222a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b0256a78d58b6d5f7a53400b19e7747d2983fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" />, the grasshopper jumps to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/7/107c7c8e5a64d81ed24331e510b777b7d08345b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" />, which is the symmetric point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b0256a78d58b6d5f7a53400b19e7747d2983fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" /> with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. Then the grasshopper jumps to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/9/9090f2e6bd5da465fea10a8c755d64e9185f61f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> which is the symmetric point of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/7/107c7c8e5a64d81ed24331e510b777b7d08345b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" /> with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and so on. Compare the distance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f87574947eecd302ba2d136ae87aa3b03b81f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_0P_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/9/a1959187164749ca908afa04472ca348cd81f353.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_0P_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/e/5ee4e5b25187f45e9cfa54eb61d6b4b858455045.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\in N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2001 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_2\">Day 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be a positive integer, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/2/4c28242522f23e896074dc89612847f8317911d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> be a real number. Consider the equation:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/0/a10529df5c75836665db01d0d8bf3ae96ab0caf9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^{n}(x_i^2+(a-x_i)^2)= na^2\\]\" width=\"199\" height=\"47\" />\nHow many solutions (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/2/2d2719960d803a38ff2560599c978b4acac5fbe7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1, x_2 \\cdots , x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"100\" height=\"11\" />) does this equation have, such that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/1/8b167df83780d55ba5dfb9c67b13a0fda5d96fd2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0 \\leq x_i \\leq a, i \\in N^+\\]\" width=\"145\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2001 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Find the value of the sum:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/b/13b97ad5b59212b797cd833ceef0381d0e2b5898.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^{2001} [\\sqrt{i}]\\]\" width=\"55\" height=\"50\" />\nwhere <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/9/97988f3618289185c731de2299e17e1b84bef42d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ {x} ]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" /> denotes the greatest integer which does not exceed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2001 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/0/b10d5ee88ffc7d59f9c282b366953fb4fa4051f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> be a semicircle with centre <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />.A circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70b97eb4ad6e4e7a5a97e2547d9ed6e965960d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> with centre <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is drawn, tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/0/b10d5ee88ffc7d59f9c282b366953fb4fa4051f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />, and tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. A semicircle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/4/7f4caea56d945d0b6e49701b42ce06e0fb92e663.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> is drawn, with centre <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/0/b10d5ee88ffc7d59f9c282b366953fb4fa4051f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> and to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70b97eb4ad6e4e7a5a97e2547d9ed6e965960d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />. A circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/5/b65e6facfe122c182fe14d503aeace2c52a9739d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> with centre <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is drawn, internally tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/0/b10d5ee88ffc7d59f9c282b366953fb4fa4051f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> and externally tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/4/7f4caea56d945d0b6e49701b42ce06e0fb92e663.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70b97eb4ad6e4e7a5a97e2547d9ed6e965960d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/e/25e95c7e16ef158247dae7de796d859d651d5d8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OPRQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"56\" height=\"16\" /> is a rectangle.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2001 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO\" title=\"2001 Pan African MO\">2001 Pan African MO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_Pan_African_MO\" title=\"2000 Pan African MO\">2000 Pan African MO</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2001 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2001 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2001 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2001 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2001 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2001 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_Pan_African_MO\" title=\"2002 Pan African MO\">2002 Pan African MO</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pan_African_MO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"Pan African MO Problems and Solutions\"> All Pan African MO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017190652\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.029 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.043 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 303/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 904/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 78/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8693/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.798      1 Template:Pan_African_MO_box\n100.00%    6.798      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:17891:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017190652 and revision id 112527. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}